  verification/results/verify-20260620T064341474739Z-fact-the-v2-covariantly-damped-maxwell-d.json:10:  "summary": "Correct. The cited stage-3 proof uses the verified covariantly damped Maxwell-Debye model from the predecessor fact and the source TM sign conventions. For the physical Maxwell-Debye half-space, the Laplace-Fourier symbol gives H_x=-ik_y E/(mu s), H_y=nu_0 E/(mu s), nu_0^2=k_y^2+mu s^2 A(s), hence Y_0^2=A(s)/mu+k_y^2/(mu^2 s^2). For the constant x-layer v2 model with rho_x=rho>0 and rho_y=0, the same symbol gives P=chi E/(1+tau(s+rho)), H_x=-ik_y E/(mu s), H_y=nu E/(mu(s+rho)), nu^2=mu(s+rho)^2 A_rho(s)+k_y^2(s+rho)/s, hence Y_rho^2=A_rho(s)/mu+k_y^2/(mu^2 s(s+rho)). Subtracting gives exactly -rho[chi tau/(mu(1+tau(s+rho))(1+tau s))+k_y^2/(mu^2 s^2(s+rho))], matching the fact file and the boxed formula in the proof artifact. Since this expression is not identically zero for rho>0 under the stated positive Debye parameters, the admittance mismatch is generically nonzero and the continuous planar-interface reflection coefficient is generically nonzero. The claim is scoped to this planar constant-coefficient x-interface test and does not overclaim more.",
  verification/results/verify-20260620T064341474739Z-fact-the-v2-covariantly-damped-maxwell-d.json:11:  "critical_errors": [],
  verification/results/verify-20260620T064341474739Z-fact-the-v2-covariantly-damped-maxwell-d.json:12:  "gaps": [],
  verification/results/verify-20260620T022411192181Z-fact-the-covariantly-damped-alpha-1-maxw.json:7:  "verdict": "accepted",
  verification/results/verify-20260620T022411192181Z-fact-the-covariantly-damped-alpha-1-maxw.json:8:  "passed": true,
  verification/results/verify-20260620T022411192181Z-fact-the-covariantly-damped-alpha-1-maxw.json:9:  "strict_verdict": "correct",
  verification/results/verify-20260620T022411192181Z-fact-the-covariantly-damped-alpha-1-maxw.json:10:  "summary": "Correct within the stated claim scope. The cited fact and proof define a modified covariantly damped alpha=1 Maxwell-Debye absorbing-layer model with variables E, H_x, H_y, P, nonnegative time-independent rho_x,rho_y, rho=rho_x+rho_y, and D_rho=partial_t+rho. Multiplying the field equations by E,H_x,H_y gives the energy derivative plus the nonnegative electric and magnetic damping terms; the Maxwell principal part integrates to the boundary flux int_dOmega E(H_y n_x - H_x n_y) ds, which vanishes under PEC E=0. The covariant Debye law P+tau D_rho P=chi E gives E D_rho P=(2 chi)^{-1} partial_t(P^2)+rho chi^{-1}P^2+tau chi^{-1}|D_rho P|^2, so the proposed positive energy has exactly the displayed monotone identity. The predecessor facts about the original source model are verified and are used only as context/motivation for the repair; the artifact clearly states that the covariantly damped model is a modified absorbing model, not an algebraically identical proof for the old eight-variable unsplit PML and not a proof of exact perfect matching.",
  verification/results/verify-20260620T022411192181Z-fact-the-covariantly-damped-alpha-1-maxw.json:11:  "critical_errors": [],
  verification/results/verify-20260620T022411192181Z-fact-the-covariantly-damped-alpha-1-maxw.json:12:  "gaps": [],
